 "description": "<p>The round-pin charger for the toy generation that used 2.5-millimeter audio-style jacks: USB on one end, the mono pin on the other, and compatibility with every toy in the drawer that charges through a small round port. A lost original cable is the commonest way these toys retire; this is the resurrection part.</p>\n<p>The wire is built to spec rather than to price: eleven copper strands inside a 3.5-millimeter line, a 17.4-millimeter pin, and a full meter of reach from USB source to nightstand. Cable length is the difference between charging where you use and charging where you can.</p>\n<p>For toy owners diagnosing a sudden dead unit, check the port shape first — a small round hole means this cable class, and a replacement costs a fraction of any toy it revives.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Type: USB to 2.5 mm audio mono pin</li>\n<li>Line length: 1 meter</li>\n<li>Line thickness: 3.5 mm</li>\n<li>Wiring: 11 copper strands</li>\n<li>Pin length: 17.4 mm</li>\n</ul>\n<p>One meter of copper for the round-port generation.</p>\n",
 "short_description": "<p>USB to 2.5mm mono pin charger cable with 1-meter length, 11-strand copper wiring and 17.4 mm pin for round-port toys.</p>\n",
